{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"35194564a23d4664","name":"card_event_capitulation","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Germany/NavalWarfare/events/card_event_capitulation","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"CAPITULATION","text":"All enemy units are Converted into ROUTED TROOPS.","flavorText":"During the early years of WWII, the German military achieved a series of rapid victories that forced multiple countries and armies to surrender. In 1939, Poland was divided after both German and Soviet attacks. In 1940, Denmark capitulated within hours, followed by Norway, which surrendered after two months of resistance. Belgium, the Netherlands, and Luxembourg also fell quickly. France, after a swift and devastating German campaign, signed an armistice in June 1940, leading to occupation. Later, Yugoslavia and Greece were overrun in the Balkans campaign of 1941, each surrendering after brief, intense fighting. Numerous other forces, including parts of the Soviet army during Operation Barbarossa, also capitulated during the German advance. Each surrender expanded German control across Europe, setting the stage for the next phases of the war. The wave of capitulations demonstrated both the power of the German military and the vulnerability of countries caught unprepared for modern warfare.","faction":"Germany","type":"order","rarity":"Unique","cost":9,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_capitulation","title":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_capitulation_title","SourceString":"CAPITULATION","LocalizedString":"CAPITULATION"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Germany","kredits":9,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_capitulation_text","SourceString":"All enemy units are Converted into ROUTED TROOPS.","LocalizedString":"All enemy units are Converted into ROUTED TROOPS."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_capitulation_history","SourceString":"During the early years of WWII, the German military achieved a series of rapid victories that forced multiple countries and armies to surrender. In 1939, Poland was divided after both German and Soviet attacks. In 1940, Denmark capitulated within hours, followed by Norway, which surrendered after two months of resistance. Belgium, the Netherlands, and Luxembourg also fell quickly. France, after a swift and devastating German campaign, signed an armistice in June 1940, leading to occupation. Later, Yugoslavia and Greece were overrun in the Balkans campaign of 1941, each surrendering after brief, intense fighting. Numerous other forces, including parts of the Soviet army during Operation Barbarossa, also capitulated during the German advance. Each surrender expanded German control across Europe, setting the stage for the next phases of the war. The wave of capitulations demonstrated both the power of the German military and the vulnerability of countries caught unprepared for modern warfare.","LocalizedString":"During the early years of WWII, the German military achieved a series of rapid victories that forced multiple countries and armies to surrender. In 1939, Poland was divided after both German and Soviet attacks. In 1940, Denmark capitulated within hours, followed by Norway, which surrendered after two months of resistance. Belgium, the Netherlands, and Luxembourg also fell quickly. France, after a swift and devastating German campaign, signed an armistice in June 1940, leading to occupation. Later, Yugoslavia and Greece were overrun in the Balkans campaign of 1941, each surrendering after brief, intense fighting. Numerous other forces, including parts of the Soviet army during Operation Barbarossa, also capitulated during the German advance. Each surrender expanded German control across Europe, setting the stage for the next phases of the war. The wave of capitulations demonstrated both the power of the German military and the vulnerability of countries caught unprepared for modern warfare."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::NavalWarfare","extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Convert"],"draftBaseWeight":0.8,"spawnCardName":"card_unit_routed_troops","soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Reinforcements'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Misc/Reinforcements.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Germany/NavalWarfare/t_capitulation.t_capitulation","SubPathString":""},"artist":"German WWII Poster","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/CAPITULATION.CAPITULATION","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":353.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_capitulation_photo","SourceString":"German soldiers standing in front of a pile of Belgian rifles and helmets on 29 May 1940, the day after Belgium's surrender.","LocalizedString":"German soldiers standing in front of a pile of Belgian rifles and helmets on 29 May 1940, the day after Belgium's surrender."},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/BP_AttackOrder.BP_AttackOrder_C","SubPathString":""},"isDirectDamage":true},"variables":[{"name":"unitsToConvert","type":"TArray<int32>","direction":"in"}],"functions":[{"name":"ExecuteUbergraph_card_event_capitulation","owner":"card_event_capitulation_C","params":[{"name":"EntryPoint","type":"int32","direction":"in"}],"pure":false,"event":false,"flags":"FUNC_Final | FUNC_UbergraphFunction | FUNC_HasDefaults","locals":[{"name":"CallFunc_Array_Length_ReturnValue","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"Temp_int_Array_Index_Variable","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_Greater_IntInt_ReturnValue","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"Temp_int_Loop_Counter_Variable","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_Add_IntInt_ReturnValue","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"K2Node_Event_targetCard","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"in